{
 "comment": "A snapshot of what each hwtests program reports on the current emulator (compat/browser.mjs), per config: test and subtest counts and the first failures as [test, source line, FNV-1a of the hwtest failure message]. Every field must match: a regression gate on the known failures. The pass/fail verdict of each subtest comes from the hardware values compiled into the hwtests binaries. jitBlocks: the smallest count of JIT blocks compiled by each program's JIT run seen so far (2026-11-09); a JIT run must compile at least 60 % of it (counts vary between runs with cpu=dual timing; over 5 runs: gxtest_clipping 72 to 130, cputest_srawix 69 to 171, cputest_nan 185 to 240). For the small programs most of these blocks are libogc's start-up, so the floor proves the JIT ran, not that every test loop compiled.",
 "notes": {
  "gxtest_clipping": "7 of 16 steps fail (compat/decode-failures.mjs decodes the messages): steps 1, 2, 3, 4 and 6 draw outside the viewport inside the guard band, where the hardware draws pixels and our software renderer clips to the viewport; steps 11 and 12 put z very slightly behind w, which the hardware's non-IEEE z+w treats as on the plane (drawn). Whether unpatched Dolphin's software renderer behaves the same is NOT verified: ours carries patches (0004, 0009, 0012, 0016, 0017, 0020, 0021, 0196).",
  "gxtest_rasterization": "514 of 519 fail (first 10 decoded by compat/decode-failures.mjs, all pinned by the fingerprint): the hardware samples a pixel near x = 7/12 (0.5833) of the sub-pixel sweep; our software renderer's sample point is elsewhere. NOT verified on unpatched Dolphin.",
  "efbpoke": "Our own probe (expected values deduced from the GX documentation and libogc, not measured on a console). Checks 2 and 3 fail: CPU pokes of the EFB have no effect on our software renderer; upstream Dolphin's SWEFBInterface::PokeColor is an empty function (Source/Core/VideoBackends/Software/SWEfbInterface.cpp), not verified by running unpatched Dolphin. Peeks and drawing match the hardware rules (RGBA6 expanded by repeating the top bits).",
  "cputest_fprf": "FPRF off by default (Config::MAIN_FPRF).",
  "cputest_nan": "ps_sum0/ps_sum1 quiet the signalling NaN they pass through.",
  "cputest_ni": "NI: the hardware flushes a result that is tiny before rounding.",
  "cputest_pairedmove": "Paired-single moves after lfd: the hardware rounds ps0's mantissa to single and truncates ps1's; ps_res/ps_rsqrte estimate edge cases.",
  "battest": "Our own test: architectural BAT rules (PowerPC 750 manual), not values measured on a console.",
  "cardtest": "Our own test through libogc's CARD API, one CARD_Write per sector: libogc's multi-sector write stops after the first sector (card.c __write_callback), on hardware as on the emulator.",
  "vitest": "Our own test: expected field rates computed from libogc's VI timing table (lines per field, 858 or 864 clocks per line at 13.5 MHz), not measured on a console."
 },
